Server environments including basic administration, maintenance, and troubleshooting. Test network connectivity, validate configurations, and perform network diagnostics. Monitor network device logs and alert systems to identify and respond to issues proactively. Document troubleshooting steps, solutions, and resolutions for knowledge base and audit purposes. Provide incident response and coordination with other departments and external vendors when necessary. Perform routine network maintenance activities and device health checks. Maintain and update network documentation and device configurations. Install, configure, and setup network equipment including cabling, switches, routers, firewalls, and physical infrastructure. Support Azure infrastructure, Microsoft 365 and cloud services as needed. Participate in other IT infrastructure related projects and tasks as needed. Provide tier-2 and tier-3 escalated support, managing and resolving tickets sent to the infrastructure queue. Serve as the lead technical resource for the India IT team, offering technical mentorship, guidance and knowledge sharing to junior staff. \n Requirements for Successful Candidate Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or related field. 10 years of experience in network administration or IT infrastructure support. Working knowledge of networking concepts including TCP/IP, switches, routers, firewalls, VLANs, and DNS/DHCP. Experience with network troubleshooting tools and diagnostics. Hands-on experience with network hardware including switches, routers, and firewalls. Experience with Windows Server administration. Foundational knowledge of Azure cloud services and infrastructure. Experience with wireless networking.). Strong troubleshooting and analytical skills with methodical problem-solving approach. Clear communication skills with ability to explain technical issues and solutions to non-technical users. Strong documentation skills and attention to detail. Ability 